WHAT THIS PROVES, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT.

Proven: a fresh 'git clone' of this repository, with no build artefacts, no
bin/ or obj/, and no local edits, restores its own packages, builds every one
of the eleven projects at zero warnings, and passes the guardrails and both
test suites - including the integration suite, which runs against the real
pinned MariaDB 10.4.32 (ADR-002) and never a substitute.

NOT proven, and deliberately not claimed: a clean MACHINE. This run reuses
this host's %ProgramData%\MerchandisingSystem\config\*.json, its XAMPP
MariaDB instance, and its installed .NET SDK. A clone that had to create
those from nothing is what scripts/bootstrap.ps1 exists for, and proving it
on a machine the author has never configured is a Phase 6 exit criterion
(plan.md section 7, promoted by ADR-012) - not this one. Recording the
distinction here because 'clean clone' and 'clean machine' are one word apart
and the weaker claim is the one this run supports.

